message: "If you use this work, please cite it as shown below."
authors:
  - family-names: Tan
    given-names: Jun Liang
    email: junliang.tan@student.uq.edu.au
    affiliation: University of Queensland
title: "QLTO: Quantum Landscape Tunneling Optimization"
version: "1.0"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.17834056"
url: "https://github.com/poig/self-research"
abstract: |
  This repository contains self-research on quantum variational optimization: QLTO, a gradient estimator on a logarithmic parameter register applied to device Hamiltonian calibration; a theory strand on single-ancilla coherent feedback with its algebraic core machine-checked in Lean 4; and earlier exploratory work on Feigenbaum universality in quantum measurement dynamics.
keywords:
  - quantum computing
  - variational quantum algorithms
  - gradient estimation
  - quantum device calibration
  - coherent feedback
  - formal verification
  - Feigenbaum
